# VERDICT 2026-09-04: PROMOTED 12:05 (commit c4085b3) - identical to production cluster.env; kept for the record.
# Means over two passes: structured 68.6, prose 40.9 harness / 40.2 by hand, c4 201 (177/225), @1400 58.9,
# code 50.5, prefill 2151/2181 (flat), long-context essay decode 35.1 (100k) / 36.2 (200k) vs 43.8 / 42.5
# at k=3. Decision and reasons: bench-results/2026-09-04-adaptive-k.md section Decision, docs/adaptive-k.md.
# Adaptive speculative draft length per request (2026-09-04, docs/adaptive-k.md).
# Purpose: keep the k=5 gains on structured / code / four-stream decode (2026-09-04 sweep:
# +16% / +7% / +53%) without the k=5 prose loss (-10..-19%), by letting the SCHEDULER truncate
# each request's drafts to 3 when that request's recent acceptance is low and keep 5 when it is
# high. The drafter always drafts SPEC_TOKENS=5 (one fused pass, fixed shape); the verify batch
# is already variable-length per request in this build; the scheduler runs in the single
# engine-core process, so the decision is identical on every TP rank.
# Mechanism: node/patches/adaptive_k_scheduler.py bind-mounted at /opt/tp4 and selected with
# --scheduler-cls (no image file shadowed). Knobs: VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_* (see the module docstring);
# default mode per-request, k 3/5, up/down 0.55/0.45, alpha 0.3, optimistic seed.
# CUDA graphs: a FULL decode graph is used only on a step whose per-request token count equals
# a CAPTURED decode_query_len; by default only SPEC_TOKENS+1 = 6 is captured, so any step at
# k=3 (4 tokens/req) would run PIECEWISE in BOTH modes. The dynamic-SD table below
# (num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size, [start,end,K] ranges, first start = 1) has two consumers:
#   - the RUNNER captures one FULL decode-graph family per K it lists (gpu/cudagraph_utils.py:196-216;
#     config/vllm.py:952-960 keeps FULL graphs on the V2 runner) and never uses it for the actual K;
#   - the SCHEDULER (production runs AsyncScheduler: dflash counts as an Eagle-type method,
#     config/vllm.py:1190-1239) sizes its draft placeholders from it (scheduler.py:1203-1205 ->
#     async_scheduler.py:23-25): the stock scheduler would verify 5 drafts at batch size 1 and 3 at 2-6.
# This scheduler (a subclass of AsyncScheduler) replaces the placeholder length per request right
# after that hand-out, so the scheduler-side effect is neutralised and only the graph capture remains.
# Effect: 4- and 6-token uniform decode graphs both exist:
#   per-request mode  -> FULL on steps where every request has the same k, PIECEWISE on mixed steps
#   batch-uniform     -> FULL on decode steps, except steps carrying a prefill chunk (never uniform,
#                        worker/utils.py:671-677) and a resumed request's first step (see below)
# Side effect of the table: the base stops padding resumed requests with [-1]*k placeholders
# (scheduler.py:892-905); such a request schedules one token without drafts on its first step
# (a PIECEWISE step, nothing to observe there).
# The KV lookahead reserves k_max+1 slots per decode step (over-reservation when truncating).
# Rank-0 log must show: the init line with num_speculative_tokens=5 and the
# num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size table, vLLM's custom-scheduler warning,
# "adaptive-k: AdaptiveKScheduler active (...) engine_k=5 async=True ...", and every 200 verify steps
# "adaptive-k: tracked=... decisions lo/hi=...". Graph descriptors are logged at DEBUG only.
# Compare against k=3 production (docs/gate.md § Baseline 2026-09-04) AND the k=5 arm
# (bench-results/2026-09-04-night-windows.md § W-B). Promotion rule: prose >= k=3 -3%,
# structured/code/c4/@1400 >= k=5 -3%, prefill flat, two passes.
# Rollback: ./tp4ctl restart without TP4_ENV (~20 min). Requires the SPEC_EXTRA_JSON-era launcher
# (preflight checks every -v source) and `TP4_ENV=experiments/2026-09-04-adaptive-k.env ./scripts/deploy.sh`.
SPEC_TOKENS=5
# Async scheduling stays ON (production default for dflash); the class requires it and disables
# itself otherwise. (The launcher never passes --no-async-scheduling: ASYNC_SCHEDULING=0 is inert.)
# Dynamic-SD table: capture decode graphs for K=5 (6 tokens/req) and K=3 (4 tokens/req).
SPEC_EXTRA_JSON='"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,1,5],[2,6,3]]'
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory=17179869184 --moe-backend triton --scheduler-cls adaptive_k_scheduler.AdaptiveKScheduler"
# EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV REPLACES the cluster.env value: the production MoE JSON mount is repeated here.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV='-v $HOME/tp4/moe-configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:ro -v $HOME/patches/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:/opt/tp4/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:ro -e PYTHONPATH=/opt/tp4 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_MODE=per-request'
